			 CogSci Courseware Project
			 Philosophy Department
			 University of Maryland
           		 College Park, MD 20742




                        COMPUTATION THEORY PACKAGE
                        --------------------------

PCOMP is a set of onscreen simulator/interpreters and editors for three
classical types of abstract models of computation:  (a) TM* for Turing
machines (includes Universal Turing machine);  (b) RAM* for simplified
von Neumann architecture random-access machines; and (c) AB* for abacus/
register machines.  Capable of million-step operations.  Users with no
computer science background can construct, run, and debug a wide variety
of types of programs.  For teaching fundamentals of the theory of
computation in a maximally student-friendly way.

Equipment:  PCOMP runs on a bottom of the line IBM PC or compatible machine --
black & white, monochrome, or color.  Requires 256K RAM, 360K of diskette
space.

PCOMP creates ASCII files (any wordprocessor can read and/or modify them).
Files can be on disk in B-drive; to access files in B-drive, filename is
preceded by "B:".

PCOMP needs no special installation procedure, and is invoked by typing the
command PCOMP at the DOS prompt.
